nodecode-cash-desk is a rewrite of FutureInvoked's FutureInvoked/cash-desk:

  https://github.com/FutureInvoked/cash-desk
  commit 26d5fabe5f50f250e5dc72c0751adbdb3625f732
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 FutureInvoked (LICENSE)

The Python plugin is rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell
contract: its ledger, CSV importers, matching rule, reminder ladder, Figure
Lock and team-approval flow are reimplemented, with money as whole cents and
dates as day numbers rather than Python Decimals and dates. The ten tools,
the section's meaning (sender, language, currency, IBAN, date order, small
balances, import folders, outbox) and the "nothing is sent without a person
approving exactly this text" rule are kept.

Left out: IMAP sync (the bank statement is a CSV the person exports), SMTP
sending (approved letters are written as .eml files for the mail client),
the Hermes desktop page, the Czech keyword reply classifier (the model passes
the reply kind) and the optional reply guard over the agent's own messages.
